eSPX

High-requests-per-second Advertising Technology tracker and billing. Stateless ingestion (gnet), Redis-backed filters, async settlement to Postgres and ClickHouse, JSON admin API in management (legacy HTMX deprecated for self-hosted).

Services: tracker, processor, management, auth, payment, billing, notifier (gRPC/Hypertext Transfer Protocol), Invalid Traffic detector (ivt-detector), fraud-scorer (cold path), edge Nginx/OpenResty Lua. Binaries under cmd/.

Service Level Agreement & budgets

Tracker (`ad_http_request_duration_seconds`, Go handler): p95 < 50 ms, p99 < 80 ms, hard ceiling 100 ms.

Production: `FILTER_TIMEOUT_MS` <= 100; development default 5000 ms.

Redis unified-filter Lua p99 < 10 ms per shard (blocks shard while running).

Geo filter p99 < 10 us (sampled). Real-Time Bidding `RunAuction` p99 < 15 us; p99 candidates scanned < 500.

Hot-path fraud accumulator + boost snapshot: incremental < 500 us per `FilterEngine.Check`; `BenchmarkFilterFraudBoost` ~90 ns, 0 allocs/op.

`GetShard` (StaticSlot): ~5.6 ns, 0 allocs/op.

Load-test abort: control-cohort p99 > 80 ms for 30 s or budget invariant violation.

Budget invariant: `current_spend <= budget_limit` in Postgres; spend tests use `AssertBudgetInvariant` (+/-1 micro-unit).

Stack

Hot path: Go 1.25+, gnet/v2, pgx/v5 + sqlc, ClickHouse, 4 standalone Redis masters (production; StaticSlotSharder, not Cluster), embedded Lua, vtproto (`make proto`), MaxMind, Prometheus.

Cold path: stdlib net/http, JSON `/api/v1`, gRPC (auth, payment, settlement, billing, notifier). Legacy HTMX fragments deprecated — see `docs/SELF_HOSTED.md`. Fraud scoring in `internal/fraudscoring` + `cmd/fraud-scorer` only - tracker must not import it.

Layout

internal/campaignmodel: shared hot-path types - Campaign, Event, BudgetManager, CampaignRegistry.

internal/ingestion: hot path - handler, track_core, FilterEngine, Lua scripts, StaticSlotSharder, stream processor, sqlc store (`internal/ingestion/sqlc`).

internal/fraudscoring: LightGBM + Isolation Forest ensemble, microbatch, optional ONNX (`-tags fraudscoring_onnx`). Scores land in Redis `ml:score:boost:{campaign_id}` via processor or fraud-scorer outbox.

internal/clickhouse/migrate: ClickHouse analytics Data Definition Language only (do not confuse with `cmd/processor`).

internal/management: single flat `package management` (one deployable). Navigate by filename tag: `blacklist_janitor.go`, `service_fraud.go`, `handler_delivery.go`. Only `pb/` subdir allowed.

internal/management/api_*.go: cold-path JSON `/api/v1` - `api_billing_handlers.go`, `api_ops_handlers.go`, ...; wire via `api_register.go`. No subfolders.

pkg/coldpath: cold-path Hypertext Transfer Protocol/JavaScript Object Notation/pagination helpers for management, auth, payment.

cmd/processor: stream consumers, sync worker, partition manager, optional fraud microbatcher.

deploy/nginx/lua/access_check.lua: edge blacklist, shard pick - must match Go StaticSlot routing.

Scripts layout: `scripts/local-dev` (compose stack), `scripts/load-test`, `scripts/perf-gate`, `scripts/chaos-drills`, `scripts/edge-tuning`, `scripts/redis-ops`, `scripts/fraud-scoring`, `scripts/k8s`, `scripts/lib`.

Redis: crc32(campaign_id) -> 1024 slots -> shard table. Shard 0 only: pub/sub (`campaigns:update`), auth lockout, brand creatives. Budget/filter keys shard by campaign_id. Edge rate limit composite key: campaign_id + user_id, fallback Internet Protocol address.

Hot path (internal/ingestion only)

Zero heap alloc per request on parse, filter, respond. Struct align size-desc; Structure of Arrays where it helps. No reflection, channels, defer in hot loops. Lock-free atomics, Multi-Producer Single-Consumer rings, batching.

Interfaces / closures: passing concrete structs as `interface{}` or `any` on hot path is forbidden - forces heap escape. Closures (`func()`) in request-processing loops are forbidden - no inlining, heap-allocated capture context. Higher-order callbacks for readability are cold-path only.

String concat: forbid `+` on strings in hot loops - each `+` allocates. Use pre-sized byte buffers (`[]byte` with known cap), stack-fixed `[N]byte`, or append into a reused buffer; never `fmt.Sprintf` or `strings.Builder` per request.

Static mapping: forbid `sync.Map` on hot path - interface boxing + key hashing overhead. Slot-to-shard routing (StaticSlotSharder): flat `[1024]uint8` table, updates via lock-free atomics (`sync/atomic`); readers load atomically, no map lookup.

Atomics / false sharing: hot global structs (StaticSlotSharder, metric registries) pad contended atomics with `_ [56]byte` or `cpu.CacheLinePad` between fields updated by different cores - unpaded adjacent atomics cause Level 1/Level 2 cache-line invalidation across cores.

Ingest: vtproto pools; byte-slice parse (`requests_parse.go`). unsafe.String/unsafe.Slice: zero-copy view lifetime must not exceed the gnet read frame; values needed beyond that frame (async settlement, queues) require explicit `copy()` into owned storage. `runtime.KeepAlive` at conversion boundaries. Bounds Check Elimination: before every indexed access `buf[i]` on gnet/vtproto buffers, emit an early abort `if len(buf) <= i { return ErrMalformed }` so the compiler eliminates `runtime.panicIndex` from assembly - a single check at loop entry is insufficient.

gnet: connContext per connection (no global sync.Pool on request path). PinnedWorkerPool pins parse+filter by campaign hash. Deterministic Finite Automaton HTTP/1.1 scanner on ring buffer.

Filters (Go, before Lua): emergency breaker -> fraud/geo (MaxMind, fail-open) -> schedule -> fraud-score boost (`GetFraudScoreBoosts()` snapshot, 0 allocs) -> Lua tier B/C (one EvalSha: budget, frequency cap, deduplication, rate, time to click). Monotonic filter deadline propagates to Redis client timeout.

Telemetry: FraudStreamWriter and LatencyRing are lossy - fixed buffers, drop on overflow, pre-bound metric labels.

Isolate hot-path pools from User Interface/HTML. Low-complexity functions for inlining.

Cold path

Idiomatic Go, stdlib-first. Postgres: explicit pgx pools, pgx.Batch, transaction isolation. ClickHouse: buffered batch inserts. Outbox in management for Redis side effects. Invalid Traffic detector: ClickHouse batch writes blacklist/outbox. fraud-scorer: model registry watcher, feature reads, ensemble scoring writes management outbox (`ML_SCORE_BOOST`, `ML_GHOST_IVT`, `ML_BLACKLIST_ADD`, `ML_MODEL_VERSION`).

Runtime

Tune Goroutines/Machines/Processors. No dynamic append on hot paths; pre-cap slices or stack-fixed arrays.

Garbage Collection profile: request memory comes from gnet ring buffers and vtproto pools - tune Garbage Collection for peak requests per second, not default latency. Set `debug.SetMemoryLimit` (or `GOMEMLIMIT`) to cap heap; keep `GOGC` at 100-200, or disable (`GOGC=off`) when Random Access Memory headroom is large. Goal: fewer, shorter Stop-The-World pauses during traffic spikes; avoid Garbage Collection fighting pre-pooled allocations.

Style

Brief, direct, senior Go audience. No fluff, emojis (except Telegram alerts), American Standard Code for Information Interchange art, decorative prefixes, all-caps logs.

Docs

Client-facing: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/DEVELOPMENT.md. Agent engineering rules: `.cursor/rules/guidelines-index.mdc` and scoped `*.mdc` (code-style, hot-path, load-test-bpf, data-layer, …).

Dev BPF infrastructure: `make bpf-dev` (or `scripts/local-dev/bpf_setup.sh`) builds `deploy/dev/bpf/loadtest_probe.o` and `bin/bpf-collector`. Enable on load tests with `ESPX_BPF_PROBE=1` (see .env.example).

Output

Hot-path changes: working code, table-driven benchmarks (`go test -bench -benchmem`), verify 0 allocs/op on touched paths; run `make test-alloc-gate`. Note escape-analysis or inlining impact only on perf-critical changes.
